WEBVTT

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.000
What about the explosion?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.940
It was a bluff.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.510
Who are you?

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:25.700
Why are you doing horrible things?

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.180
I'm Sherry LeBlanc.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:36.150
I was testing your abilities.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.470
A female D-Wheeler…

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:41.590
I’m sorry that I tricked you.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:46.300
But I'm here to take you, Yusei Fudo.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:49.590
I won't let any other team have you!

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:14.100
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:19.630
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:24.110
Don't look back and keep going

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:29.940
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:34.920
There's no need to fear

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:42.590
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:48.600
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:54.370
Streak to the infinite future

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:59.770
Dreams surpass their limits

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:07.880
And will lead you to a bright place

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:40.260
What Lies Inside the Wind

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.210
You're here to take me?

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.910
What do you mean?

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.400
I want you to join my team.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.820
You'll enter the WRGP as part 
of my team and win it all.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.100
What?

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.870
I don't need your answer today.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:01.690
This duel is to say hello.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.020
Let’s have fun.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.040
Wait!

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.620
Get off, Aki!  It’s too dangerous!

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.600
No!  Let me keep riding!

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.880
I want to see your Riding Duel.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:19.010
I feel that there's an important 
moment that I need to see.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:21.610
I understand.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.610
Hold on tight!

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:28.490
I knew he'd come.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.060
My turn!

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.460
I summon the Tuner Monster Turbo Synchron!

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:44.670
Level 1 Turbo Synchron 
tunes Level 5 Junk Warrior!

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:48.370
The bond comes together 
to call forth a new power!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.870
Become the path that lights the way!

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.710
Synchro Summon!

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.050
Roar, Turbo Warrior!

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.720
Turbo Warrior attacks Chevalier de Fleur!

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.820
I activate Turbo Warrior’s effect!

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:09.180
When this monster attacks a Level 6-or-higher 
monster, your monster’s attack points are halved.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.220
Incredible!

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:15.370
This destructive effect takes 
advantage of a monster's high Level!

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.730
Accel Slash!

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.910
Why isn’t it destroyed?

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:26.010
The trap card For Our Dreams!

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:31.720
By sending a monster on my field to the 
graveyard, my monster isn't destroyed in battle!

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:38.890
By surviving this battle, Chevalier de 
Fleur’s attack points return to normal.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:43.130
That means Turbo Warrior 
will be destroyed next turn.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.220
I flip over my trap card!

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.600
Synchro Out!

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.280
By returning a Synchro Monster 
on my field to the Extra Deck...

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:55.070
...its Synchro Material Monsters in the 
graveyard return until the End Phase.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.540
Why?

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:00.540
Even if you bring back those monsters, 
Chevalier de Fleur has higher attack points.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:04.280
He’s planning to Synchro Summon again.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:10.020
That means Yusei's set card 
is probably Urgent Tuning.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:16.380
He’ll use Urgent Tuning to resurrect Turbo 
Warrior and attack Chevalier de Fleur again.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:24.700
But Chevalier de Fleur's effect negates your 
spell or trap card's effect and destroys it.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:27.170
Yusei hasn't forgotten about that.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.910
He must be setting up an even greater combo!

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:33.560
Yusei, what are you planning to do?

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.530
Chevalier de Fleur’s effect 
can only be used once per turn!

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:39.820
What will you do?

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.530
Keep trying to surprise me.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.240
I have a strategy that's greater than yours!

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:49.330
I won't use Chevalier de Fleur’s 
effect on Synchro Out!

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:54.490
Appear, Turbo Synchron and Junk Warrior!

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.120
Next, I flip over my trap card Urgent Tuning!

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:05.120
Just like I thought!

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.860
I won’t let you Synchro Summon!

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:08.960
I activate Chevalier de Fleur’s effect!

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:10.610
I destroy your trap card!

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.050
Now you don’t have any traps.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:19.100
You might have a spell.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:23.980
Due to the card's destruction, 
I flip over my trap card!

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.490
Chain Close!

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:30.170
You can’t activate spell or 
trap cards until the End Phase.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:31.940
Incredible.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.860
She shut Yusei down.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:37.700
Chevalier de Fleur will attack next 
turn and destroy Yusei’s monster

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.500
because it has low attack points.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.640
I anticipated this.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.310
I knew you would do this.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:48.600
Turbo Synchron attacks Chevalier de Fleur!

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.860
Why, Yusei?

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:54.600
I activate Turbo Synchron’s effect!

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:57.440
The attack target switches 
to defense position!

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.330
But what can you do with Turbo Synchron?  
It only has 100 attack points!

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.600
He only has 100 life points left.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:13.900
Yusei, do you realize what you did?

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.460
Yusei…

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:20.510
I activate Turbo Synchron’s effect!

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:24.430
I can Special Summon a monster 
from my hand whose attack points

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:28.130
are equal or less than the 
damage I took from the attack!

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.830
I summon Junk Collector!

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:35.960
I activate Junk Collector’s effect!

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:42.130
By removing this card and a trap card in my 
graveyard from play, the removed trap activates!

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:46.410
I select Urgent Tuning in my 
graveyard to Synchro Summon!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.640
No way!

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:51.950
Even though he can’t use spell or trap 
cards, he can still activate monster effects!

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:57.990
Level 1 Turbo Synchron 
tunes Level 5 Junk Warrior!

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:05.740
Resurrect, Turbo Warrior!

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:13.700
I see.

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:16.370
You'll do whatever it 
takes to Synchro Summon.

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:20.840
Turbo Warrior attacks Chevalier 
de Fleur in defense position!

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.380
Accel Slash!

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.140
I end my turn.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:31.920
Yusei is having fun even 
though he’s in a fight.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:33.940
Her too.

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:38.970
It’s different than his 
duel against me in the past.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:40.100
Against Jack and Crow...

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:44.070
Even against Sherry, who he’s 
only met for the first time...

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:48.040
Yusei is dueling from a 
place deep within his heart.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.490
Yusei, even though you 
destroyed Chevalier de Fleur,

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:55.060
you shouldn't have left yourself 
with only 100 life points.

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:59.680
With Speed World 2, when I 
have 4 or more Speed Counters,

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:04.390
I can deal 800 points of damage 
for every Speed Spell in my hand.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:10.090
I have 4 Speed Counters 
and zero cards in my hand.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:13.340
Your fate depends on my draw.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:16.570
The instant I draw a Speed Spell, you lose.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.130
Oh no!

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:23.140
Yusei, you're past the 
Riding Duel's safety line.

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:28.070
You exposed yourself to a world of 
speed that's side-by-side with death.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.500
A world of speed…

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:43.650
My turn!

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:51.620
I summon Sacred Knight's Shield 
Bearer in defense position!

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:55.390
It wasn’t a Speed Spell.

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:57.910
I activate Sacred Knight's 
Shield Bearer’s effect!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:04.020
By removing a Sacred Knight in my graveyard 
from play, I can draw one card from my deck!

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:05.330
Oh no!

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.820
She gets to draw again!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:16.130
I set one card and end my turn.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:21.830
I had many chances, but fate abandoned me.

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:24.440
I want you even more.

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:25.800
Hey!

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:31.240
Yusei, why do you duel?

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:34.420
Why are you entering the WRGP?

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:40.430
I'm entering the Grand 
Prix to find a new goal.

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:42.690
That means you have nothing.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.190
Why do we duel…

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:49.400
What are you trying to say?

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:51.790
I have a goal.

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:55.770
I have a huge goal called revenge.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:58.740
Revenge…

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:16.820
Revenge…

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:18.450
That’s right.

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:28.210
The LeBlanc family was in the card business 
for ages.  I was the only daughter.

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:32.650
I had a happy life with my kind parents.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:41.180
However…

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:46.870
My parents' smiles soon 
vanished from their faces.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:52.920
A corporation was trying to buy the 
company that my father managed.

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:55.090
My father refused.

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:08.870
Then…

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:40.850
Papa!  Mama!

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:09.490
However…

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:13.800
Since I survived, the 
company chased after me.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:21.670
I fled around the world and learned that a 
certain organization was behind the company.

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:25.800
It was Iliaster.

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.280
Iliaster!

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:30.250
I heard that name before.

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:31.960
Me too.

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:36.050
Divine said they were Arcadia 
Movement's evil enemy.

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:41.410
Iliaster is a legendary organization that 
surpasses the ideas of good and evil.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:45.530
They will do anything to eliminate 
anyone who gets in their way.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:48.170
Such as killing my family.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.140
Horrible…

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:56.580
I began to understand why 
they’re chasing me.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:08.100
Yusei, help me.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:12.630
Iliaster is pulling the 
strings of the upcoming WRGP.

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:14.140
What?

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:19.050
I want to win the WRGP so that 
I can get closer to them!

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:25.660
I need to know what Iliaster 
is planning to do!

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:29.400
I want to know why my 
parents had to be killed!

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:31.920
That’s why I need you, Yusei!

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:36.070
But Jack and Crow are Yusei's 
teammates!  That's why-

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:37.020
I didn’t ask you!

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:38.340
Wait a second!

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:41.020
You don’t know anything about Yusei!

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.030
Yes, I do!

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:46.720
Due to these few turns, we 
now understand each other.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:52.190
The speed and wind inform me about 
the rumblings in Yusei’s heart.

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:54.490
And my heart too.

00:14:55.290 --> 00:15:00.250
That’s something only Riding 
Duelists can understand!

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:05.980
Just like this speed, I’m 
battling at the edge.

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:10.130
Yusei, don’t you also 
desire this type of dueling?

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:15.000
If we battle together, you'll 
be able to find your goal!

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:15.860
I…

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:18.880
I don’t think it's a bad proposal.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.490
Think carefully.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.470
It’s your turn.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:27.140
What’s with her?

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:30.470
My turn!

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:34.850
I activate the Field Spell 
Speed World 2's effect.

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:39.150
By removing 7 Speed 
Counters, I draw one card!

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:43.260
I summon the Tuner Monster Drill Synchron!

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:47.820
Turbo Warrior attacks Sacred 
Knight's Shield Bearer!

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:49.360
Accel Slash!

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:54.240
I activate Drill Synchron’s effect!

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:59.940
When my monster attacks your monster in 
defense position, you take piercing damage!

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:08.550
And when you take damage from this 
effect, I draw one card from my deck!

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.280
I flip over my trap card Liberty at Last!

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:14.690
When a monster on my field 
is destroyed in battle,

00:16:14.690 --> 00:16:17.390
all monsters on the field 
return to our decks!

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:23.530
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:26.170
Yusei’s field is wide open.

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:30.860
If she draws a Speed Spell or a 
monster next turn, Yusei will lose.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:35.420
My turn!

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.840
I summon Sacred Knight Joan!

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:43.250
A monster card!

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:49.850
Due to Sacred Knight Joan’s effect, it 
loses 300 attack points when it attacks.

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:52.460
Sacred Knight Joan attacks you directly!

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:54.630
Sacred Decision!

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:59.400
I flip over the trap card Synchro Spirits!

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:02.400
By removing one Synchro Monster 
in my graveyard from play,

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:05.160
I can Special Summon its 
Synchro Material Monsters!

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:09.010
I remove Junk Warrior from play 
to resurrect Junk Synchron

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:11.160
and Speed Warrior in defense position!

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.130
Interesting.

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:19.380
I end my turn!

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:25.370
She's incredible.  Such 
fast offense and defense.

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:27.140
These two are...

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:33.550
Is Sherry right?

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:38.970
That a Riding Duel allows two people 
to understand each other’s souls?

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:42.970
That means Yusei knows what's in her heart.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:45.410
It's probably true.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:52.410
Within the speed and the wind, 
Yusei battled and felt the anger,

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:56.690
screams, pain and joy of 
his friends and rivals!

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:02.040
It only exists within the 
speed of a Riding Duel.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:05.330
Only D-Wheelers can 
understand this sensation!

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:09.900
My turn!

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:14.970
I activate Speed Spell - High 
Speed Crash from my hand!

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:17.560
When I have 2 or more Speed Counters,

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:21.460
I destroy one card on my field and 
another card on either of our fields!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:26.080
You’re planning to destroy Sacred Knight 
Joan by sacrificing your set card.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:32.930
But if an effect destroys Joan, I can add 
one spell card in my graveyard to my hand.

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.130
A Speed Spell.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:38.600
I destroy my set card and Speed Warrior!

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:39.680
What?

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:40.990
Speed Warrior?

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:44.280
At this moment, I activate 
the trap card Starlight Road!

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:45.410
That’s what you were aiming for!

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:50.610
With Starlight Road, when two or more 
cards on my field are destroyed...

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:54.180
...that effect is negated, and I 
Special Summon Stardust Dragon!

00:18:58.550 --> 00:18:59.600
Yusei!

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:00.180
That’s…

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:07.700
Yusei Fudo, I won’t let you enter the WRGP!

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:10.330
I'll punish you for defying me!

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:14.750
Leave it to me, Yusei!

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:16.590
Aki, what are you doing?

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.170
I'll summon it!

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:18.800
Aki!

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:22.570
It's the only thing I can 
do for Yusei right now.

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:25.190
Please, Stardust Dragon!

00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:35.010
A psychic duelist!

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:47.930
Damn!

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.610
Well done, Mizoguchi.

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.570
Yusei Fudo…

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:27.100
I like the look in your eyes.

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:33.390
Yusei, if we kept dueling...

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:37.510
Your Stardust Dragon would've 
destroyed Sacred Knight Joan.

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:41.050
Then Speed Warrior would've 
attacked me directly.

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:44.460
But I still would've had 50 life points left.

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:45.860
You didn't beat me yet.

00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:46.850
Yeah.

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:51.960
It all depends on what you draw next, Sherry.

00:20:57.300 --> 00:20:58.580
I won’t draw.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.520
The world of speed never ends.

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:02.910
Neither does what’s ahead of us.

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:06.310
Let’s meet again, Yusei.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.640
And you too.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:12.580
You're interesting.

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:22.190
I also want to know.

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:26.110
By becoming the wind among the speed, I'll 
be able to understand Yusei’s heart.

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:28.930
But in order to do that, 
I have to do Riding Duels.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:41.980
Why do you duel?

00:22:09.360 --> 00:22:14.040
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:19.050
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:23.950
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:23.950 --> 00:22:28.960
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:33.830
The cruel god tests us

00:22:34.130 --> 00:22:40.770
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:44.640
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:44.640 --> 00:22:50.510
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:54.410
Bond is the proper word

00:22:54.410 --> 00:23:00.390
As we fight, we understand each other

00:23:00.390 --> 00:23:03.360
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:05.590
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:05.590 --> 00:23:10.270
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:10.560 --> 00:23:13.130
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:16.600
You want to party until the morning

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:19.840
At our special place
